<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_37" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_37">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_37" name="BPMN-37 | Customer Review Submission" processRef="Process_37" />
    <bpmn:participant id="Cloudinary_37" name="Cloudinary — optional review-photo storage" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="PhotoRequest_37" sourceRef="Upload_37" targetRef="Cloudinary_37" name="Validated optional review photos" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="PhotoResponse_37" sourceRef="Cloudinary_37" targetRef="Upload_37" name="Stored photo references or failure" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_37" name="Customer Review Submission" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-37, BPMN-38 and subscription eligibility clarification; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.18 FR-REV-01-07, BR-21, NFR-SEC-03-04,08-09 and documented Cloudinary review-photo storage; supporting NFR-REL-01-03,05. Website: index.html loads app/orders.js O.reviewable/reviewed and review-item, app/product.js rating/comment/demo-photo composer/handleReviewSubmit, app/owner-reviews.js R.capture/public, app/account-state.js customer ownership and subscription state. Existing BPMN-26/30/33/35/36 and catalog process boundaries reviewed. SRS primary: up to three optional supported photos (prototype has two demo slots), one enrollment-level subscription review only after all four weekly fulfillments, and no separate weekly review. FR-REV-01/03/07 item association applies to standard/cake purchased items; subscription uses original owned enrollment/purchase as review unit per BR-21, not a fabricated weekly-item review. This is an explicitly visible SRS alignment rule rather than silently adopting prototype behavior. No additional customer receipt-button gate is imposed beyond documented completion; preview O.reviewable requires receivedAt for some non-subscription orders. Authentication is a BPMN-26 precondition; recheck customer/private purchase access at protected save. All local eligibility/content/photo/save/recovery decisions visible on main diagram. Internal Customer/System lane links are sequence flows, optional Cloudinary exchange is cross-pool message flow. Recipe, production/completion, subscription progress and authentication are not rerun to submit feedback; BPMN-14/16/17 and BPMN-05 provide existing completion evidence. Owner inspection/hide/unhide is BPMN-38 and is not a prerequisite approval step or automated classifier. No review-edit/delete feature, sentiment/profanity filtering, external notification or owner payout is invented. A valid rating is required (prototype five-star integer scale); comment is optional and photo count may be zero. Submitted review is associated with its purchased item or enrollment and customer; simultaneous retries cannot create duplicates. Known successful save is reused; other existing review does not authorize a second review. Recovery retains draft, revalidates eligibility/current identity, reuses already stored matching photo references where safe and avoids duplicate uploads/reviews; these are proposed reliability safeguards, not claims the preview already implements them.</bpmn:documentation>
